&lt;h1&gt;vLLM v0.25.1&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Highlights&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This release features 2 commits from 2 contributors (1 new)!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v0.25.1 is a patch release containing two targeted bug fixes on top of v0.25.0.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bug Fixes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Avoid blocking model launching when no system FFmpeg is available for TorchCodec&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4830103553&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/47888&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47888/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47888&quot;&gt;#47888&lt;/a&gt;). Previously &lt;code&gt;import torchcodec&lt;/code&gt; raised a &lt;code&gt;RuntimeError&lt;/code&gt; at import time when system FFmpeg was missing, which blocked startup (e.g. &lt;code&gt;vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct&lt;/code&gt;) even when TorchCodec was not in use. The error is now deferred to runtime so it only surfaces if TorchCodec is actually needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guard mixed-dtype allreduce RMSNorm quant fusions&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4861605008&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/48330&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/vllm-project/vllm/pull/48330/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/48330&quot;&gt;#48330&lt;/a&gt;). The fused FlashInfer allreduce + RMSNorm + static-quantization patterns could match graphs where the activation and RMSNorm weight dtypes differ (e.g. a BF16 residual stream with an FP32 Gemma/Qwen-style RMSNorm weight in NVFP4 models), corrupting the hidden state and producing garbage output such as repeated &lt;code&gt;!!!!!&lt;/code&gt; tokens. A dtype-match guard now routes incompatible mixed-dtype graphs to the safe path, while same-dtype models retain the full allreduce + RMSNorm + quant fusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Contributors&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/Isotr0py/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/Isotr0py&quot;&gt;@Isotr0py&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/hugo-cen/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/hugo-cen&quot;&gt;@hugo-cen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
